From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:59:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] tool: aggregate the commit-time sweep into the headroom
 answer

Turns the commit_now baseline plus the commit_at runs into the four things
T10 section 5 asks for: the rescue rate over the seeds the fixed setpoint
fails, the working commit times and cheapest one per rescued seed, the shape
of the feasible commit set, and the reverse cost on seeds the baseline already
completes.

The shape matters as much as the rate. If one commit time rescues every seed
the report says so explicitly -- a constant is not a policy, and that is gate B
telling the round to stop rather than train.

Written against the schema evaluate_arrival_condition_script already emits, so
the analysis costs no round of its own once the data lands.

